invariant: INV-73
file: src/handshake_record.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: hsr_feed writes the handshake's bytes into cfg.buf and leaves
  buf_written_len where it was, so tlsi_give_back_buf wipes none of them
  and the next handshake that takes the buffer finds this one's
  plaintext. The loop test fills each buffer with a sentinel and requires
  a run of zero bytes, then the sentinel alone (docs/decisions.md 249).

--- old
    if (t->buf_written_len < t->pt_len) {
        t->buf_written_len = t->pt_len;
    }
    CH_ASSERT(t->pt_len <= t->buf_written_len && t->buf_written_len <= t->cfg.buf_len);
--- new
